:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/DEVCLS'.Device class (DEVCLS)
:P.The device class for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TAP, *OPT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/RSRCNAME'.Resource name (RSRCNAME)
:P.The hardware resource name, as WRKHDWRSC shows it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*VRT:EPK.
:PD.Virtual.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/TYPE'.Device type (TYPE)
:P.The device type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RSRCNAME.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/ONLINE'.Online at IPL (ONLINE)
:P.Whether the device or line is varied on when the system starts (IPL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is varied on at IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It stays varied off until someone varies it on.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/UNLOADWAIT'.Unload wait time (UNLOADWAIT)
:P.The unload wait time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSGEN:EPK.
:PD.The value the system generates.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/MAXDEVTIME'.Maximum device wait time (MAXDEVTIME)
:P.The maximum device wait time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSGEN:EPK.
:PD.The value the system generates.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/RSCALCPTY'.Resource allocation priority (RSCALCPTY)
:P.The resource allocation priority for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/INLMNTWAIT'.Initial mount wait time (INLMNTWAIT)
:P.The initial mount wait time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/EOVMNTWAIT'.End of volume mount wait time (EOVMNTWAIT)
:P.The end of volume mount wait time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/GENCTGID'.Generate cartridge ids (GENCTGID)
:P.The generate cartridge ids for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSGEN:EPK.
:PD.The value the system generates.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VOLID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/ROBOTDEV'.Robot device descriptions (ROBOTDEV)
:P.The robot device descriptions for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/ROBOTHOST'.Robot host (ROBOTHOST)
:P.The robot host for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/LCLINTNETA'.Local internet address (LCLINTNETA)
:P.The local internet address for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.QSYSOPR, the system operator's message queue.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVMLB/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDEVOPT.Create Device Desc (Optical) (CRTDEVOPT)
:P.Use the Create Device Desc (Optical) (CRTDEVOPT) command to create an
optical device description; RSRCNAME(*VRT) makes a virtual optical
device over an image catalog.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/DEVD'.Device description (DEVD)
:P.The device description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/RSRCNAME'.Resource name (RSRCNAME)
:P.The hardware resource name, as WRKHDWRSC shows it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*VRT:EPK.
:PD.Virtual.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/TYPE'.Device type (TYPE)
:P.The device type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RSRCNAME.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/LCLINTNETA'.Local internet address (LCLINTNETA)
:P.The local internet address for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/ONLINE'.Online at IPL (ONLINE)
:P.Whether the device or line is varied on when the system starts (IPL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is varied on at IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It stays varied off until someone varies it on.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.QSYSOPR, the system operator's message queue.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVOPT/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDEVPRT.Create Device Desc (Printer) (CRTDEVPRT)
:P.Use the Create Device Desc (Printer) (CRTDEVPRT) command to create a
printer device description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/DEVD'.Device description (DEVD)
:P.The device description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/DEVCLS'.Device class (DEVCLS)
:P.The device class for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:PT.:PK.*VRT:EPK.
:PD.Virtual.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SNPT, *LAN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/TYPE'.Device type (TYPE)
:P.The device type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IPDS:EPK.
:PD.IPDS, the intelligent printer data stream.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be one of the values F4 lists.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/MODEL'.Device model (MODEL)
:P.The device model for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/LANATTACH'.LAN attachment (LANATTACH)
:P.The LAN attachment for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IP:EPK.
:PD.TCP/IP.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LEXLINK, *USRDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/PORT'.Port number (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/ONLINE'.Online at IPL (ONLINE)
:P.Whether the device or line is varied on when the system starts (IPL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is varied on at IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It stays varied off until someone varies it on.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/PRTQLTY'.Print quality (PRTQLTY)
:P.The print quality&colon. draft, normal text or near-letter quality.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STD:EPK.
:PD.Standard.
:PT.:PK.*DRAFT:EPK.
:PD.Draft quality.
:PT.:PK.*NLQ:EPK.
:PD.Near letter quality.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/FONT'.Font (FONT)
:P.The font the printer uses.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Point size
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/FORMFEED'.Form feed (FORMFEED)
:P.How paper is fed to the printer&colon. continuous forms, cut sheets
fed by hand, or an automatic sheet feeder.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CONT:EPK.
:PD.Continuous forms.
:PT.:PK.*CUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets fed by hand.
:PT.:PK.*AUTOCUT:EPK.
:PD.Single cut sheets from a sheet feeder.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TYPE, *CONT2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/SEPDRAWER'.Separator drawer (SEPDRAWER)
:P.The separator drawer for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/SEPPGM'.Separator program (SEPPGM)
:P.The separator program for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/PRTERRMSG'.Printer error message (PRTERRMSG)
:P.The printer error message for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:PT.:PK.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.QSYSOPR, the system operator's message queue.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTLD.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSYSOPR is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/TRANSFORM'.Host print transform (TRANSFORM)
:P.Whether the host print transform converts the SCS data to the
printer's ASCII data stream.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/MFRTYPMDL'.Manufacturer type and model (MFRTYPMDL)
:P.The manufacturer type and model for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WSCST, *IBM42011, *HP4, *HP5, *HP5SI, *HPII,
*HPIID, *HPIIP, *HPIII, *HPIIID, *HPIIIP, *HPIIISI, *HPPLUS, *HPLJ4,
*IBM3812, *IBM4019.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/PPRSRC1'.Paper source 1 (PPRSRC1)
:P.The paper source 1 for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MFRTYPMDL, *LETTER, *LEGAL, *EXECUTIVE,
*LEDGER, *A3, *A4, *A5, *B4, *B5, *CONT80, *CONT132.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/PPRSRC2'.Paper source 2 (PPRSRC2)
:P.The paper source 2 for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MFRTYPMDL, *LETTER, *LEGAL, *EXECUTIVE,
*LEDGER, *A3, *A4, *A5, *B4, *B5, *CONT80, *CONT132.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/ENVELOPE'.Envelope source (ENVELOPE)
:P.The envelope source for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MFRTYPMDL, *MONARCH, *NUMBER9, *NUMBER10, *B5,
*C5, *DL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/MAXPNDRQS'.Maximum pending requests (MAXPNDRQS)
:P.The maximum pending requests for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 31.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 6 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/PRTRQSTMR'.Print request timer (PRTRQSTMR)
:P.The print request timer for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 3600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/CHRID'.Character identifier (CHRID)
:P.The graphic character set and code page of the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Graphic character set
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Code page
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/WSCST'.Workstation customizing object (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/USRDTATFM'.User data transform (USRDTATFM)
:P.The program that transforms the user data of a spooled file before it
is sent to the printer.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/USRDRVPGM'.User driver program (USRDRVPGM)
:P.The user driver program that sends spooled files when no device
writer is used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/SYSDRVPGM'.System driver program (SYSDRVPGM)
:P.The system driver program for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *HPPJLDRV, *IBMPJLDRV, *NETSTNDRV, *IBMSNMPDRV,
*IBMIPPDRV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/SECURECNN'.Secure connection (SECURECNN)
:P.Whether to secure connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVPRT/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDEVTAP.Create Device Desc (Tape) (CRTDEVTAP)
:P.Use the Create Device Desc (Tape) (CRTDEVTAP) command to create a
tape device description; RSRCNAME(*VRT) makes a virtual tape device over
an image catalog.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/DEVD'.Device description (DEVD)
:P.The device description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/TYPE'.Device type (TYPE)
:P.The device type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*VRT:EPK.
:PD.Virtual.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RSRCNAME.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/MODEL'.Device model (MODEL)
:P.The device model for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RSRCNAME.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/RSRCNAME'.Resource name (RSRCNAME)
:P.The hardware resource name, as WRKHDWRSC shows it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*VRT:EPK.
:PD.Virtual.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/SWTSET'.Switch setting (SWTSET)
:P.The switch setting for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/ONLINE'.Online at IPL (ONLINE)
:P.Whether the device or line is varied on when the system starts (IPL).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.It is varied on at IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.It stays varied off until someone varies it on.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/CTL'.Attached controller (CTL)
:P.The attached controller for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/ASSIGN'.Assign device at vary on (ASSIGN)
:P.Whether to assign device at vary on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/UNLOAD'.Unload device at vary off (UNLOAD)
:P.Whether to unload device at vary off.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.QSYSOPR, the system operator's message queue.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDEVTAP/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
